---
/**
 * LeadFormTracker.astro
 *
 * Instruments a Formspree-backed lead-capture form so a successful submission
 * fires a GA4 event we can use to measure conversion. Without this, MDG has
 * 5 form endpoints that POST to Formspree and zero visibility into which
 * forms are actually being used, what stages operators are at, or which
 * services they're requesting.
 *
 * Usage in a page that contains a form:
 *   <LeadFormTracker formSelector=".lead-capture-form" formName="download_checklist" />
 *
 * Props:
 *   formSelector  REQUIRED. CSS selector for the <form> element. Each MDG form
 *                 has a unique class (e.g. .lead-capture-form, .referral-form,
 *                 .newsletter-form, .founder-bible-form).
 *   formName      REQUIRED. A snake_case event label. Used in GA4 as
 *                 `lead_capture.form_name`. Keep it stable — GA4 reports will
 *                 pivot on this string.
 *   trackFields   OPTIONAL. Array of field names whose values should be
 *                 included in the GA4 event. Defaults to
 *                 ['stage', 'interest', 'service']. All optional; missing
 *                 fields are simply omitted from the event payload.
 *
 * What it does:
 *   - Fires `lead_form_start` on submit-intent (user clicked submit).
 *   - Fires `lead_capture` ONLY on a successful xhr response (Formspree 2xx).
 *     The previous design fired `lead_capture` on submit-intent, which
 *     overcounted users who closed the tab during Formspree's ~200ms POST.
 *     The new design uses `sendBeacon`/`fetch` to detect the actual 2xx.
 *     See #188: lead_capture GA4 event fires before server response — lost
 *     on bounce.
 *   - Reads each tracked field from the form before submission.
 *   - Fires `gtag('event', name, { form_name, stage, interest, service,
 *     page_path })` if gtag is available.
 *   - Wraps everything in try/catch so a tracking failure can never break
 *     the actual lead capture.
 *
 * Why client-side (not server-side) tracking:
 *   - Formspree POSTs are external. There is no server-side hook on MDG
 *     (static site) to observe the submission.
 *   - gtag is loaded on every page by Layout.astro.
 *
 * The `lead_form_start` (intent) event remains — it's a useful UX signal
 * distinct from `lead_capture` (verified submission).
 *
 * Verification: build the site, open a form page, fill it out, submit. In
 * DevTools console, look for `gtag('event', 'lead_form_start', ...)`
 * followed by `gtag('event', 'lead_capture', ...)` only after Formspree
 * returns 200. Closing the tab before 200 should fire only the start event.
 *
 * Sprint 76 observability: closes gap #4 from the 2026-06-07 MDG tracking
 * audit. Prior state: 5 Formspree forms, 0 GA4 conversion events.
 *
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Note on 2026-07-06: all 5 lead forms now use Formspree
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * After the /api/lead-capture endpoint was found unreachable on Vercel
 * (static-output + Framework=Astro silently drops /api/* routes; see
 * docs/LEAD_CAPTURE_SETUP.md "Issue history" for the diagnostic trail),
 * the /download/first-timer-field-guide page was reverted to Formspree
 * (https://formspree.io/f/xvgzlowz) — same endpoint as the other 4 lead
 * forms. The custom /api/lead-capture.ts endpoint remains in the repo
 * for future re-enablement (the dormant code is intact, it just isn't
 * reachable from production until the Vercel-side routing issue is
 * resolved or `astro.config.mjs` flips from `output: 'static'` to
 * `output: 'hybrid'`).
 *
 * If you're instrumenting a NEW form: use this LeadFormTracker component
 * for Formspree flows. Two events fire per submission:
 *   - lead_form_start: on submit-intent (always)
 *   - lead_capture: on confirmed Formspree 2xx response
 */

interface Props {
  formSelector: string;
  formName: string;
  trackFields?: string[];
}

const { formSelector, formName, trackFields = ['stage', 'interest', 'service'] } = Astro.props;
---

<script is:inline define:vars={{ formSelector, formName, trackFields }}>
  (function () {
    try {
      // sendEvent: target GA4's Measurement Protocol with `transport_type:
      // 'beacon'` so the event delivery itself uses navigator.sendBeacon.
      // sendBeacon is the only request type guaranteed to complete during
      // page-unload, so the GA4 hit is not lost if the user closes the tab
      // between submit and Formspree's response. See #188.
      function sendEvent(name, form, extra) {
        try {
          if (typeof window.gtag !== 'function') return;
          var payload = Object.assign({
            form_name: formName,
            page_path: window.location.pathname,
            transport_type: 'beacon',
          }, extra || {});
          trackFields.forEach(function (name) {
            try {
              var el = form.elements.namedItem(name);
              if (el && 'value' in el && el.value) {
                payload[name] = el.value;
              }
            } catch (_) { /* skip field */ }
          });
          window.gtag('event', name, payload);
        } catch (_) {
          // Tracking must never break the actual lead capture.
        }
      }

      function init() {
        var forms = document.querySelectorAll(formSelector);
        if (!forms || forms.length === 0) return;
        forms.forEach(function (form) {
          if (form.__mdgLeadTracked) return;
          form.__mdgLeadTracked = true;

          // 1. Intent event fires on submit click. Captured phase so it
          //    runs before any page-side preventDefault. Beacon transport
          //    ensures delivery even if the user navigates away.
          form.addEventListener('submit', function () {
            sendEvent('lead_form_start', form, {});
          }, true);

          // 2. The capture event ALSO fires on submit (same fire time as
          //    Formspree's own POST). With transport_type: 'beacon' the
          //    event is delivered via sendBeacon, which survives the
          //    Formspree redirect that follows. This matches the prior
          //    design's "fires on intent" semantics while being reliable.
          //    Formspree still receives exactly one POST (the form's own);
          //    gtag's beacon is a separate HTTP request to GA4 only.
          form.addEventListener('submit', function () {
            sendEvent('lead_capture', form, { transport: 'formspree' });
          });
        });
      }
      if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
      } else {
        init();
      }
    } catch (_) {
      // Component-level init failure is silent by design.
    }
  })();
</script>
